course: dictionary
lesson: 13193
title: Frustrate: cross when you cannot get your way
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Frustrate is a verb. To frustrate someone is to make them feel cross and upset because they cannot do or get what they want. When you feel this way, you feel frustrated.
explain: «Sam tried to tie his shoelace, but the knot kept slipping, and it frustrated him.» The knot stopped Sam from doing what he wanted, so he felt cross and upset. The clues are the knot that kept slipping and the word tried.
explain: Frustrate can also mean to stop a plan from working. «The rain frustrated our plans for a picnic.» The rain did not make us cross in this sentence. It stopped the picnic from happening.
explain: When you feel frustrated, you can calm down. Take a breath, ask for help, and try again. Heroes in stories often frustrate the villain's plans, so the villain cannot win.
fact: Frustrate is a verb: frustrate, frustrates, frustrated, frustrating.
fact: «Frustrated» means feeling cross and upset because you cannot do or get what you want.
fact: «Frustrating» describes something that makes you feel this way, like «a frustrating puzzle».
fact: To frustrate a plan is to stop it from working.
fact: Name the feeling, then calm it: take a breath, ask for help, or try again.
exercise: «The puzzle piece would not fit, and it frustrated Mia.» What does frustrated mean here? | Pleased and proud | *Cross and upset because the piece would not fit | Sleepy after a long day
exercise: «The storm frustrated the sailors' plan to reach the island.» What does frustrated mean here? | Painted the plan in bright colours | *Stopped the plan from working | Helped the plan to grow bigger
exercise: Which is a good way to calm down when you feel frustrated? | *Take a deep breath and ask for help | Shout at everyone in the room | Throw your book across the room | Give up and never try again
test: «The locked door frustrated the children, who could not get inside.» What does frustrated mean here? | *Cross and upset because they could not get what they wanted | Excited to play | Hungry for lunch
test: What does it mean to frustrate someone's plans? | *To stop the plans from working | To write the plans down | To help the plans grow
exam: Which sentence uses frustrate correctly? | The music frustrated the dancers, who loved every beat | The sunshine frustrated the cat, which was happy to nap | *The broken bike frustrated Ella, who could not ride to school | Frustrate means a sweet fruit that grows on trees
